<urn:atm:triage:finding/RBQA-BA-F010>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "RBQA-BA-F010" ;
  triage:title "Herdr run_blocking has no concurrency bound and duplicates BoundedBlockingBridge" ;
  triage:description "ruthless-boundary-qa phase-ending critical review @ 9f5aef2fe. Finding: Herdr's run_blocking helper (18 call sites) has no concurrency bound and duplicates the existing BoundedBlockingBridge pattern (crates/atm-daemon-bootstrap/src/router_support.rs:80-177); two additional raw spawn_blocking calls exist at received_hook_selector.rs:601 and :679. VERIFIED pre-existing on develop (17 of the 18 run_blocking uses predate Phase BA; BA added only the RSH-001 timeout wrapper, not the sites themselves). fenix's ruling: important (architecture hardening, no regression introduced by Phase BA), not critical/blocking. Fix landed on fix/phase-ba-review-2 by arch-ctm: routed the Herdr pump through a BoundedBlockingBridge-backed bridge sized to the tick budget, migrated received_hook_selector's two raw sites, deleted run_blocking entirely; HERDR_REQUEST_DEADLINE became a RequestDeadline type as a side effect. NOTE: originally drafted as finding id RBQA-F010; renamed to RBQA-BA-F010 per fenix's ruling (ATM 01M2A821M48VWSZ0JGXMA4WWZ7, 2026-09-12T07:24:38Z) because RBQA-F010 collides with a closed Phase-AI record of the same id -- the specific Herdr-bridge fix commit is review-2 32ba10f45, within the review-2 rebased frozen head 984da6c6c. fenix (ATM 01M2AFXE4KCRFRNQ60NDKCD4BN, 2026-09-12T09:41:56Z): REVIEW-2 FINAL REMAP (frozen) -- 32ba10f45 -> 30148d759; branch FROZEN, all 13 gates green at review-2 tip 0b4911c5a." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-ba" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "hardening" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
